{
  "repo": "EH3D-PHOENIX-3DP",
  "ecosystem": "eh3d",
  "tagline": "A model, a printer profile, a safe G-code and a link to the printer or to the server.",
  "description": "EH3D-PHOENIX-3DP is a set of Rust libraries and a command line program for 3D printing: it reads STL, OBJ and 3MF models and the projects other programs save as 3MF, holds a catalog of printer profiles built from public data, slices a closed model into layers with perimeters, rectilinear, grid or gyroid infill, bridges and plain supports, writes G-code for four dialects with temperature limits that refuse a value instead of cutting it down, and drives Moonraker and OctoPrint printers and the EH3D server, so far only against simulators and a socket of the same computer. A window with four tabs is written for the gui feature.",
  "columns": [
    "WHO USES IT",
    "THIS REPOSITORY",
    "WHAT IT DEPENDS ON"
  ],
